{"id":"2F","title":"Laws & Commandments of God","part":{"n":2,"title":"Relationship to God"},"url":"/law/02-relationship-to-god/2f","entries":[{"id":"2F.1","text":"We are required to always keep all of God's Law, His charge, His statutes, His commandments, and His judgments. Exod. .15:26;","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":18,"verses":"4-5,26,30"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"37"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":20,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":4,"verses":"14,40"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":6,"verses":"17,25"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":7,"verses":"11"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":8,"verses":"1,61"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":11,"verses":"1,8,32"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":13,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":26,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":29,"verses":"9"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"10,16"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":22,"verses":"5"},{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":8,"verses":"58,61"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":20,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Lev. 18:4-5, 26, 30; Lev. 19:37; Lev. 20:22; Deut 4:14, 40; Deut 6:17, 25; Deut 7:11; Deut. 8:1, 61 11; Deut 11: 1 , 8, 32; Deut 13:4; Deut 26:16; Deut 29:9; Deut 30:10, 16; Josh. 22:5; 1 Kings 8:58, 61; Ezek. 20:19."},{"id":"2F.2","text":"This is God's commandment: that we should believe on the name of His Son Jesus Christ and love one another.","refs":[{"book":"1 John","chapter":3,"verses":"23"}],"citation":"1 John 3:23."},{"id":"2F.3","text":"God loves only those who keep His commandments.","refs":[{"book":"John","chapter":14,"verses":"23"}],"citation":"John 14:23."},{"id":"2F.4","text":"Following the Commandments of God is righteous.","refs":[{"book":"Luke","chapter":1,"verses":"6"}],"citation":"Luke 1:6."},{"id":"2F.5","text":"We must obey Christ and his commandments.","refs":[{"book":"John","chapter":15,"verses":"14"},{"book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":10,"verses":"5"}],"citation":"John 15:14; 2 Cor. 10:5."},{"id":"2F.6","text":"You shall walk in all the ways of the LORD your God.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":5,"verses":"33"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":10,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":11,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":13,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":26,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":22,"verses":"5"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":119,"verses":"1,3"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":128,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Deut. 5:33; Deut 10:12; Deut 11:22; Deut 13:4; Deut 26:17; Deut 30:16; Josh. 22:5; Psa. 119:1, 3; Psa. 128:1."},{"id":"2F.7","text":"The book of the law shall not depart out of your mouth, but you shall meditate on it day and night.","refs":[{"book":"Joshua","chapter":1,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":1,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"Josh. 1:8; Psa. 1:2."},{"id":"2F.8","text":"We are to keep God's law continually for ever and ever.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":119,"verses":"44"}],"citation":"Psa. 119:44."},{"id":"2F.9","text":"Adhere to God's will, for He will try and prove you to see whether or not you will walk in His law and keep His commandments.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":16,"verses":"4"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":8,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Judges","chapter":2,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Judges","chapter":3,"verses":"1,4"},{"book":"Job","chapter":7,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":26,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":6,"verses":"27"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":17,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Exod. 16:4, Deut 8:2; Judges 2:22; Judges 3:1, 4; Job 7:18; Psa. 26:2; Jer. 6:27; Jer. 17:10."},{"id":"2F.10","text":"Whoever shall break one of the least of these commandments (of God), and so teaches others, shall be called least in the kingdom of God; but whoever keeps and teaches them, he shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Matt. 5:19."},{"id":"2F.11","text":"Walk orderly and keep the law.","refs":[{"book":"Acts","chapter":21,"verses":"24"}],"citation":"Acts 21:24."},{"id":"2F.12","text":"We know God by keeping his commandments. Thus he that claims to know God but does not keep His commandments is a liar.","refs":[{"book":"1 John","chapter":2,"verses":"4-5"}],"citation":"1 John 2:4-5."},{"id":"2F.13","text":"The law and word of God is absolute and perpetual.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":40,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Malachi","chapter":3,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":16,"verses":"17"},{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":1,"verses":"25"}],"citation":"Isa. 40:8; Mal. 3:6; Matt. 5:18; Luke 16:17; 1 Pet 1:25."},{"id":"2F.14","text":"Sin is the transgression of the law.","refs":[{"book":"1 John","chapter":3,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"1 John 3:4."},{"id":"2F.15","text":"The wages of sin is death.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":6,"verses":"23"}],"citation":"Rom. 6:23."},{"id":"2F.16","text":"Where there is no law, there is no transgression.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":4,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":5,"verses":"13"}],"citation":"Rom. 4:15; Rom. 5:13."},{"id":"2F.17","text":"The law gives knowledge of sin.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":7,"verses":"7"}],"citation":"Rom. 3:20; Rom. 7:7."},{"id":"2F.18","text":"Obedience to the commandments of God are of prime importance in our lives.","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":12,"verses":"13"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":7,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Eccl. 12:13; 1 Cor. 7:19."},{"id":"2F.19","text":"The law of God will bring blessings if obeyed.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":26,"verses":"3-12"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":7,"verses":"12-24"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":11,"verses":"13-15,26-27"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":28,"verses":"1-14"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":1,"verses":"7-8"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Luke","chapter":11,"verses":"28"}],"citation":"Lev. 26:3-12; Deut. 7:12-24; Deut. 11:13-15, 26-27; Deut. 28:1-14; Deut. 30:19 15, 19-20; Josh. 1:7-8; Isa. 1:19; Luke 11:28."},{"id":"2F.20","text":"The Law of God will bring curses and punishment if disobeyed.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":15,"verses":"26"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":26,"verses":"14-45"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":8,"verses":"19-20"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":11,"verses":"16-17,26-28"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":28,"verses":"15-68"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"1,15,19"},{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":17,"verses":"1-41"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":1,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":42,"verses":"24-25"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":5,"verses":"24-25"},{"book":"Hosea","chapter":4,"verses":"6-7"}],"citation":"Exod. 15:26; Lev. 26:14-45; Deut. 8:19-20; Deut. 11:16-17, 26-28; Deut. 28:15-68; Deut. 30:1,15, 19; 1 Kings 17:1-41; Isa. 1:20; Isa. 42:24-25; Jer. 5:24-25; Hos. 4:6- 7."},{"id":"2F.21","text":"Blessings to be brought back to a people who return to obeying God's laws.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":30,"verses":"1-10"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":7,"verses":"14"}],"citation":"Deut 30:1 -10; 2 Chron. 7:14."},{"id":"2F.22","text":"Those who forsake the law praise the wicked, but those who keep the law strive with them.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":28,"verses":"4"}],"citation":"Prov. 28:4."},{"id":"2F.23","text":"The law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient, the ungodly, for sinners, for the unholy and profane, for murders, whoremongers, homosexuals, kidnappers, liars, perjurers, and whatever else is contrary to sound doctrine.","refs":[{"book":"Galatians","chapter":3,"verses":"19"},{"book":"1 Timothy","chapter":1,"verses":"9-10"}],"citation":"Gal. 3:19; 1 Tim. 1:9-10."},{"id":"2F.24","text":"If you wish to enter into life, keep the commandments.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":19,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":22,"verses":"14"}],"citation":"Matt. 19:17; Rev. 22:14."},{"id":"2F.25","text":"If you keep the commandments, you shall abide in Christ's love.","refs":[{"book":"John","chapter":15,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"John 15:10."},{"id":"2F.26","text":"Blessed is the man who delights greatly in God's commandments.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":112,"verses":"1"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":119,"verses":"92"}],"citation":"Psa. 112:1; Psa. 119:92."},{"id":"2F.27","text":"The law has dominion over us as long as we live.","refs":[{"book":"Romans","chapter":7,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"Rom. 7:1."},{"id":"2F.28","text":"You shall not add to the word which God commanded nor take away from it.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":4,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":12,"verses":"32"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":1,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":30,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Revelation","chapter":22,"verses":"18-19"}],"citation":"Deut. 4:2; Deut. 12:32; Josh. 1:7; Prov. 30:6; Rev. 22:18-19."},{"id":"2F.29","text":"You are not to deviate from the law to the right or to the left.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":5,"verses":"32"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":1,"verses":"7"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":23,"verses":"6"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":34,"verses":"2"}],"citation":"Deut. 5:32; Josh. 1:7; Josh. 23:6; 2 Chron 34:2."},{"id":"2F.30","text":"Man cannot render perfect obedience to the law (all have sinned).","refs":[{"book":"1 Kings","chapter":8,"verses":"46"},{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":6,"verses":"36"},{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":7,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verses":"10"},{"book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verses":"23"},{"book":"James","chapter":2,"verses":"10-11"}],"citation":"1 Kings 8:46; 2 Chron. 6:36; Eccl. 7:20; Rom. 3:10; Rom. 3:23; James 2:10-11."},{"id":"2F.31","text":"We are exhorted to study the law and scriptures.","refs":[{"book":"John","chapter":5,"verses":"39"},{"book":"Acts","chapter":17,"verses":"11"},{"book":"2 Timothy","chapter":2,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"John 5; 39; Acts 17; 11; 2 Tim. 2:15."}]}